{"tool_name":"flipflop","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"flipflop","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/flipflop.html","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Discovers which isoforms of a gene are expressed in a given sample together with their abundances, based on RNA-Seq read data. It takes an alignment file in SAM format as input, and it can also discover transcripts from several samples simultaneously, increasing statistical power.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:57:50Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-10T05:27:34Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.12.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:flipflop","credit":[{"email":"elsa.bernard@mines-paristech.fr","name":"Elsa Bernard","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://projects.cbio.mines-paristech.fr/flipflop/"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/flipflop.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"},"format":[{"term":"SAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2573"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"RNA-Seq analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1255"},"format":[{"term":"GTF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2306"}]}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Splicing model analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2499"}]}],"name":"flipflop","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btu317","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Several state-of-the-art methods for isoform identification and quantification are based on '1-regularized regression, such as the Lasso. However, explicitly listing the-possibly exponentially-large set of candidate transcripts is intractable for genes with many exons. For this reason, existing approaches using the '1-penalty are either restricted to genes with few exons or only run the regression algorithm on a small set of preselected isoforms. Results: We introduce a new technique called FlipFlop, which can efficiently tackle the sparse estimation problem on the full set of candidate isoforms by using network flow optimization. Our technique removes the need of a preselection step, leading to better isoform identification while keeping a low computational cost. Experiments with synthetic and real RNA-Seq data confirm that our approach is more accurate than alternative methods and one of the fastest available. \u00a9 The Author 2014. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Bernard E."},{"name":"Jacob L."},{"name":"Mairal J."},{"name":"Vert J.P."}],"citationCount":35,"date":"2014-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Efficient RNA isoform identification and quantification from RNA-Seq data with network flows"},"pmcid":"PMC4147886","pmid":"24813214","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"RNA splicing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3320"},{"term":"RNA-seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"flipflop","home":"https://bio.tools/flipflop","license":"GPL-3.0","version":"1.12.0","summary":"Discovers which isoforms of a gene are expressed in a given sample together with their abundances, based on RNA-Seq read data. It takes an alignment file in SAM format as input, and it can also discover transcripts from several samples simultaneously, increasing statistical power.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:flipflop:1.12.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecom